---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import LangToggle from '../../../components/LangToggle.astro';

// Static default for the wiring view: MHA (32 Q heads, 32 KV heads).
// Geometry mirrored by the JS renderer — keep in sync.
const NQ = 32;
const wireQ = Array.from({ length: NQ }, (_, i) => ({
  i,
  x: 30 + 22 * i,
  cx: 39 + 22 * i,
}));
---

<Base
  title="Attention-head anatomy: MHA, MQA, GQA, MLA — Junwon Lee"
  description="Interactive anatomy of attention-head sharing: MHA, MQA, GQA and DeepSeek's Multi-head Latent Attention — head wiring, a KV-bytes calculator with real model configs, and the low-rank + decoupled-RoPE trick, matrix by matrix."
>
  <div class="att-page">
    <!-- ============ HERO ============ -->
    <section class="section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="hero-top">
          <p class="eyebrow">Study · Model anatomy</p>
          <LangToggle />
        </div>
        <h1>
          <span class="lang-en">Attention-head anatomy: one cache, four wirings</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">Attention head 해부: 하나의 cache, 네 가지 배선</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="lede">
          <span class="lang-en">
            MHA, MQA, GQA and MLA are one design decision seen from four points: how many
            query heads share each cached K/V. Turn the dial from 32 private K/V pairs down
            to a single shared latent, put real model configs through the bytes calculator,
            then open DeepSeek's Multi-head Latent Attention matrix by matrix.
          </span>
          <span class="lang-ko">
            MHA·MQA·GQA·MLA는 별개의 네 설계가 아니라 하나의 결정 — cache된 K/V 하나를
            몇 개의 query head가 공유하는가 — 를 네 지점에서 본 것이다. 32개의 전용 K/V
            pair에서 하나의 shared latent까지 다이얼을 돌려 보고, 실제 모델 config를 byte
            계산기에 넣어 본 뒤, DeepSeek의 Multi-head Latent Attention을 matrix 단위로
            열어 본다.
          </span>
        </p>

        <nav class="arc-roadmap" aria-label="Page roadmap">
          <a href="#arc-s1"><span class="arc-n">§1</span><span class="lang-en">Why the cache hurts</span><span class="lang-ko">cache가 왜 문제인가</span></a>
          <a href="#arc-s2"><span class="arc-n">§2</span><span class="lang-en">What the cache stores</span><span class="lang-ko">cache에 담기는 것</span></a>
          <a href="#arc-s3"><span class="arc-n">§3</span><span class="lang-en">Head wiring</span><span class="lang-ko">Head 배선</span></a>
          <a href="#arc-s4"><span class="arc-n">§4</span><span class="lang-en">KV-bytes calculator</span><span class="lang-ko">KV-byte 계산기</span></a>
          <a href="#arc-s5"><span class="arc-n">§5</span><span class="lang-en">MLA deep-dive</span><span class="lang-ko">MLA 딥다이브</span></a>
          <a href="#arc-s6"><span class="arc-n">§6</span><span class="lang-en">What the papers claim</span><span class="lang-ko">논문의 실제 주장</span></a>
          <a href="#arc-s7"><span class="arc-n">§7</span><span class="lang-en">Where this goes</span><span class="lang-ko">어디로 가는가</span></a>
        </nav>

        <div class="arc-prereq">
          <span class="lang-en"><strong>Before you start:</strong> you should be comfortable
            with the basic attention equation — queries, keys, values and
            softmax(QKᵀ/√d)·V. It also helps to know why GPU decoding is limited by memory
            bandwidth rather than FLOPs (<a href="/study/gpu/memory-hierarchy/">GPU memory
            hierarchy</a>) and how RoPE encodes position
            (<a href="/study/models/rope/">RoPE</a>) — §5 leans on the latter.</span>
          <span class="lang-ko"><strong>시작하기 전에:</strong> attention의 기본 수식 —
            query·key·value와 softmax(QKᵀ/√d)·V — 에는 익숙하다고 가정한다. GPU decoding이
            FLOPs가 아니라 memory bandwidth에 막히는 이유(<a
            href="/study/gpu/memory-hierarchy/">GPU memory hierarchy</a>)와 RoPE가 position을
            인코딩하는 방식(<a href="/study/models/rope/">RoPE</a>)을 알면 좋다 — 특히 §5가
            후자에 기댄다.</span>
        </div>

        <div class="config-note">
          <span class="config-lead">
            <span class="lang-en">Verified reference configs used on this page (official
              config.json / papers):</span>
            <span class="lang-ko">이 페이지에서 사용하는 검증된 기준 config (공식
              config.json / 논문):</span>
          </span>
          <span class="tag">Llama-2-7B — MHA · 32Q/32KV</span>
          <span class="tag">Llama-3-8B — GQA · 32Q/8KV</span>
          <span class="tag">Mistral-7B — GQA · 32Q/8KV</span>
          <span class="tag accent">DeepSeek-V2/V3 — MLA · c 512 + rope 64</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ §1 · THE ITCH ============ -->
    <section class="section-tight" id="arc-s1">
      <div class="container">
        <h2 class="viz-h arc-heading">
          <span class="arc-num">§1</span>
          <span class="lang-en">Why the cache hurts — the problem before any mechanism</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">cache가 왜 문제인가 — 메커니즘 이전의 문제</span>
        </h2>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>
            <span class="lang-en">
              An autoregressive LLM generates one token at a time, and each new token must
              attend to every token that came before it. To avoid recomputing the past at
              every step, the model stores per-token state — the KV cache — and re-reads it
              on every single generated token. The weights are a fixed cost; the cache grows
              with context length, and again with every sequence served in parallel.
            </span>
            <span class="lang-ko">
              autoregressive LLM은 token을 하나씩 생성하고, 새 token은 앞선 모든 token을
              attend해야 한다. 매 step마다 과거를 다시 계산하지 않으려고 모델은 token별
              상태 — KV cache — 를 저장해 두고, token 하나를 생성할 때마다 전부 다시
              읽는다. weight는 고정 비용이지만 cache는 context 길이에 비례해 자라고, 동시에
              서빙하는 sequence 수만큼 다시 배로 자란다.
            </span>
          </p>
          <p>
            <span class="lang-en">
              Put numbers on it. Llama-2-7B in FP16 has about 13.5 GB of weights — fixed.
              Its KV cache costs 512 KB per token, so one 8K-context sequence adds 4 GB.
              Serve a batch of 16 and the cache alone is 64 GB — nearly five times the
              weights — and an 80 GB GPU is full before its compute units are ever the
              bottleneck. That is the itch: the cache, not the weights, caps how many
              sequences a GPU can serve at long context.
            </span>
            <span class="lang-ko">
              숫자로 보자. FP16의 Llama-2-7B는 weight가 약 13.5 GB — 고정이다. KV cache는
              token당 512 KB이므로 8K context sequence 하나가 4 GB를 더한다. batch 16을
              서빙하면 cache만 64 GB — weight의 거의 5배 — 이고, 80 GB GPU는 연산 유닛이
              병목이 되기도 전에 메모리부터 가득 찬다. 이것이 가려운 지점이다: 긴 context에서
              GPU가 서빙할 수 있는 sequence 수를 막는 것은 weight가 아니라 cache다.
            </span>
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="viz-frame">
          <div class="att-scroll">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 760 210" role="img"
              aria-label="Memory budget of Llama-2-7B at 8K context: 13.5 GB of fixed weights versus a KV cache that grows from 4 GB at batch 1 to 64 GB at batch 16"
              style="width:100%; height:auto; min-width:680px;">
              <text class="rowlab" x="20" y="22">Llama-2-7B · MHA · FP16 · 8K context — 512 KB of cache per token per sequence</text>
              <text class="ssub" x="20" y="56" text-anchor="start">weights</text>
              <rect x="150" y="44" width="114" height="16" rx="3" fill="var(--swatch-slate)"></rect>
              <text class="smono" x="272" y="57">13.5 GB — fixed</text>
              <text class="ssub" x="20" y="94" text-anchor="start">KV · batch 1</text>
              <rect x="150" y="82" width="34" height="16" rx="3" fill="var(--accent)" opacity="0.55"></rect>
              <text class="smono" x="192" y="95">4 GB</text>
              <text class="ssub" x="20" y="132" text-anchor="start">KV · batch 8</text>
              <rect x="150" y="120" width="270" height="16" rx="3" fill="var(--accent)" opacity="0.75"></rect>
              <text class="smono" x="428" y="133">32 GB</text>
              <text class="ssub" x="20" y="170" text-anchor="start">KV · batch 16</text>
              <rect x="150" y="158" width="540" height="16" rx="3" fill="var(--accent)"></rect>
              <text class="smono" x="150" y="196">64 GB — cache ≈ 5 × weights; with weights, an 80 GB GPU is full</text>
            </svg>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="arc-takeaway">
          <span class="arc-takeaway-label"><span class="lang-en">Takeaway</span><span class="lang-ko">핵심 한 줄</span></span>
          <span class="lang-en">At long context the KV cache — not the weights — is the
            memory bill that caps batch size, so shrinking it is worth real architecture
            changes.</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">긴 context에서 batch 크기를 막는 메모리 비용은 weight가
            아니라 KV cache다 — 그래서 이것을 줄이는 일은 아키텍처를 바꿀 만한 가치가
            있다.</span>
        </div>
        <p class="arc-question">
          <span class="lang-en">Where do those 512 KB per token actually come from — what
            exactly does the cache store?</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">token당 512 KB는 정확히 어디서 나오는가 — cache에는 무엇이
            저장되나?</span>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ §2 · FOUNDATIONS ============ -->
    <section class="section-tight" id="arc-s2">
      <div class="container">
        <h2 class="viz-h arc-heading">
          <span class="arc-num">§2</span>
          <span class="lang-en">What the cache stores — heads, K/V, and one formula</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">cache에 담기는 것 — head, K/V, 그리고 공식 하나</span>
        </h2>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>
            <span class="lang-en">
              Inside every layer, every token is projected into three vectors: a query, a
              key and a value. Multi-head attention runs this several times in parallel —
              Llama-2-7B uses 32 heads of dimension 128 — so each head can attend to a
              different aspect of the context. When token t is generated, its query must be
              scored against the <em>keys of all previous tokens</em>, and the resulting
              weights average their <em>values</em>. Those past keys and values never
              change, so recomputing them every step would be pure waste: the model computes
              them once and caches them. That is the KV cache — one K and one V vector per
              head, per layer, for every token seen so far.
            </span>
            <span class="lang-ko">
              모든 layer에서 모든 token은 세 vector로 projection된다: query, key, value.
              multi-head attention은 이것을 병렬로 여러 번 돌린다 — Llama-2-7B는 dimension
              128짜리 head 32개 — 각 head가 context의 다른 측면을 보게 하기 위해서다.
              token t를 생성할 때 그 query는 <em>앞선 모든 token의 key</em>와 score를 내고,
              그 가중치로 <em>value</em>들을 평균한다. 과거의 key·value는 변하지 않으므로
              매 step 다시 계산하는 것은 순수한 낭비다: 한 번 계산해서 cache한다. 이것이
              KV cache다 — 지금까지 본 모든 token에 대해 head당·layer당 K 하나와 V 하나.
            </span>
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="viz-frame">
          <div class="att-scroll">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 760 230" role="img"
              aria-label="One decode step: the new token produces q, k and v; k and v are appended to the KV cache; q reads every cached key and value"
              style="width:100%; height:auto; min-width:680px;">
              <defs>
                <marker id="arrFnd" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
                  <path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" fill="#87857c"></path>
                </marker>
              </defs>
              <rect class="sbox" x="20" y="80" width="130" height="46" rx="9"></rect>
              <text class="stitle sm" x="85" y="100" text-anchor="middle">new token t</text>
              <text class="smono" x="85" y="118" text-anchor="middle">hidden state h_t</text>
              <line class="flowline" x1="150" y1="92" x2="216" y2="48" marker-end="url(#arrFnd)"></line>
              <line class="flowline" x1="150" y1="103" x2="216" y2="103" marker-end="url(#arrFnd)"></line>
              <line class="flowline" x1="150" y1="114" x2="216" y2="158" marker-end="url(#arrFnd)"></line>
              <rect class="sbox" x="220" y="24" width="120" height="40" rx="9"></rect>
              <text class="stitle sm" x="280" y="41" text-anchor="middle">q_t — query</text>
              <text class="smono" x="280" y="56" text-anchor="middle">used once, not cached</text>
              <rect class="sbox sbox-accent" x="220" y="84" width="120" height="40" rx="9"></rect>
              <text class="stitle sm" x="280" y="101" text-anchor="middle">k_t — key</text>
              <text class="smono" x="280" y="116" text-anchor="middle">appended to cache</text>
              <rect class="sbox sbox-accent" x="220" y="144" width="120" height="40" rx="9"></rect>
              <text class="stitle sm" x="280" y="161" text-anchor="middle">v_t — value</text>
              <text class="smono" x="280" y="176" text-anchor="middle">appended to cache</text>
              <line class="flowline" x1="340" y1="104" x2="416" y2="118" marker-end="url(#arrFnd)"></line>
              <line class="flowline" x1="340" y1="164" x2="416" y2="146" marker-end="url(#arrFnd)"></line>
              <rect class="sbox sbox-cache" x="420" y="96" width="320" height="60" rx="10"></rect>
              <text class="stitle sm" x="436" y="120">KV cache — grows by one row per token</text>
              <text class="smono" x="436" y="140">[k_1 v_1] [k_2 v_2] … [k_t v_t] · per head · per layer</text>
              <path class="flowline" d="M340,44 H580 V92" fill="none" marker-end="url(#arrFnd)"></path>
              <text class="ssub" x="352" y="38">q_t scores EVERY cached key, then averages the values</text>
              <text class="smono" x="20" y="216">cache cost per token = 2 × layers × kv_heads × head_dim × bytes/elt   (the 2 is K and V)</text>
            </svg>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="prose">
          <p>
            <span class="lang-en">
              That one formula prices everything on this page. Per token, the cache costs
              2 · layers · kv_heads · head_dim · bytes — and each factor is an attack
              surface. Bytes-per-element is quantization's territory; sequence length is
              eviction's and hybrid attention's. This page is about the
              <em>kv_heads</em> factor: for Llama-2-7B the product is
              2 · 32 · 32 · 128 · 2 B = 512 KB per token, and 32 of those factors are head
              count.
            </span>
            <span class="lang-ko">
              이 공식 하나가 이 페이지의 모든 것을 값 매긴다. token당 cache 비용은
              2 · layers · kv_heads · head_dim · bytes — 그리고 인자 하나하나가 공략
              지점이다. bytes-per-element는 quantization의 영역, sequence 길이는
              eviction과 hybrid attention의 영역이다. 이 페이지는 <em>kv_heads</em> 인자를
              다룬다: Llama-2-7B에서 곱은 2 · 32 · 32 · 128 · 2 B = 512 KB/token이고, 그중
              32 하나가 head 수다.
            </span>
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="arc-takeaway">
          <span class="arc-takeaway-label"><span class="lang-en">Takeaway</span><span class="lang-ko">핵심 한 줄</span></span>
          <span class="lang-en">The cache is K and V vectors per head, per layer, per token
            — bytes/token = 2 · layers · kv_heads · head_dim · bytes, and every factor in
            that product is a lever.</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">cache는 head당·layer당·token당 K와 V vector이고, 비용은
            2 · layers · kv_heads · head_dim · bytes다 — 이 곱의 모든 인자가 레버다.</span>
        </div>
        <p class="arc-question">
          <span class="lang-en">32 query heads each carrying a private K/V pair — do they
            really all need their own?</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">query head 32개가 각자 전용 K/V pair를 가진다 — 정말 전부
            자기 것이 필요할까?</span>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ §3 · HEAD WIRING ============ -->
    <section class="section-tight" id="arc-s3">
      <div class="container">
        <h2 class="viz-h arc-heading">
          <span class="arc-num">§3</span>
          <span class="lang-en">Head wiring — one dial from MHA to MQA</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">Head 배선 — MHA에서 MQA까지 하나의 다이얼</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="arc-bridge">
          <span class="lang-en">We now have the price formula, and kv_heads is its most
            exposed factor. The insight behind ten years of attention variants is that this
            factor is a free dial: MHA, GQA and MQA are not three designs but three
            positions of it. This section makes that dial literal.</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">이제 가격 공식이 있고, 그중 가장 공략하기 쉬운 인자가
            kv_heads다. 지난 attention 변형들의 통찰은 이 인자가 자유롭게 돌릴 수 있는
            다이얼이라는 것이다: MHA·GQA·MQA는 세 가지 설계가 아니라 다이얼의 세 위치다.
            이 섹션은 그 다이얼을 문자 그대로 보여준다.</span>
        </p>
        <p class="viz-sub">
          <span class="lang-en">Hover a query head to see exactly which cached K/V it reads.
            Drag the KV-heads dial: 32 is MHA, 1 is MQA, everything between is GQA. MLA
            replaces the K/V row with a shared latent.</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">query head 위에 hover하면 그 head가 읽는 cache된 K/V가
            표시된다. KV-heads 다이얼을 움직여 보자: 32면 MHA, 1이면 MQA, 그 사이는 전부
            GQA다. MLA는 K/V 행 자체를 shared latent로 바꾼다.</span>
        </p>

        <div class="viz-frame">
          <div class="wire-controls">
            <div class="mode-row" role="group" aria-label="Attention variant">
              <button class="mode-btn on" data-var="mha" type="button">MHA</button>
              <button class="mode-btn" data-var="gqa" type="button">GQA</button>
              <button class="mode-btn" data-var="mqa" type="button">MQA</button>
              <button class="mode-btn" data-var="mla" type="button">MLA</button>
            </div>
            <div class="dial-wrap" id="dialWrap">
              <label class="dial-label" for="kvDial">
                <span class="lang-en">KV heads</span><span class="lang-ko">KV heads</span>
              </label>
              <span class="dial-col">
                <input type="range" id="kvDial" min="0" max="5" step="1" value="0" />
                <span class="dial-ticks" aria-hidden="true">
                  <span>32</span><span>16</span><span>8</span><span>4</span><span>2</span><span>1</span>
                </span>
              </span>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="att-scroll">
            <svg id="wireSvgEl" viewBox="0 0 760 300" role="img"
              aria-label="Wiring between 32 query heads and their K/V sources for MHA, GQA, MQA and MLA"
              style="width:100%; height:auto; min-width:740px;">
              <g id="wireDyn">
                <text class="rowlab" x="30" y="40">Q heads — 32 × d_h 128</text>
                <text class="rowlab" x="30" y="256">K/V heads — what the cache stores</text>
                {wireQ.map((q) => (
                  <line class="wline" data-line={q.i} x1={q.cx} y1="96" x2={q.cx} y2="196" />
                ))}
                {wireQ.map((q) => (
                  <rect class="qh" data-q={q.i} x={q.x} y="64" width="18" height="30" rx="4" />
                ))}
                {wireQ.map((q) => (
                  <rect class="kvh" data-kv={q.i} x={q.x} y="198" width="18" height="30" rx="4" />
                ))}
              </g>
            </svg>
          </div>

          <div class="wire-stats" id="wireStats">
            <span class="stat-chip">32 KV heads</span>
            <span class="stat-chip">2 × 32 × 128 = <b>8,192</b> elts / token / layer</span>
            <span class="stat-chip"><b>16 KB</b> FP16 / token / layer</span>
          </div>

          <p class="cap" id="wireCap">
            <span class="lang-en">MHA — every query head owns a private K/V pair. Nothing is
              shared: 32 K and 32 V vectors are cached per token per layer, 8,192 elements
              (16 KB in FP16). This is the quality reference all sharing schemes are measured
              against.</span>
            <span class="lang-ko">MHA — 모든 query head가 전용 K/V pair를 가진다. 아무것도
              공유되지 않으므로 token·layer당 K 32개와 V 32개, 8,192개 원소(FP16 기준
              16 KB)가 cache된다. 모든 sharing 방식의 품질 기준점이다.</span>
          </p>

          <noscript>
            <p class="viz-sub">
              <span class="lang-en">With JavaScript enabled this diagram morphs between MHA,
                GQA, MQA and MLA; the static view shows MHA (32 K/V heads).</span>
              <span class="lang-ko">JavaScript가 켜져 있으면 이 다이어그램은 MHA·GQA·MQA·MLA
                사이를 전환한다. 정적 화면은 MHA(32 K/V heads)를 보여준다.</span>
            </p>
          </noscript>
        </div>

        <div class="prose">
          <p>
            <span class="lang-en">
              The wiring view makes the family relationship literal: fix 32 query heads and
              slide the number of K/V heads. At 32 every query head has a private K/V pair
              (MHA); at 1 a single K/V head serves all of them (MQA); every stop between is
              GQA with group size 32/kv. Nothing else about attention changes — same scores,
              same softmax, same output projection. The only thing the dial moves is how many
              K and V vectors must be written to, stored in, and read back from the KV cache.
            </span>
            <span class="lang-ko">
              배선 뷰는 이 가족 관계를 문자 그대로 보여준다: query head 32개를 고정하고 K/V
              head 수만 움직여 보자. 32면 head마다 전용 K/V pair(MHA), 1이면 하나의 K/V
              head가 전부를 담당(MQA), 그 사이 모든 지점이 group 크기 32/kv의 GQA다.
              attention의 다른 부분은 아무것도 변하지 않는다 — score도, softmax도, output
              projection도 같다. 다이얼이 움직이는 것은 오직 KV cache에 쓰고, 저장하고,
              다시 읽어야 하는 K·V vector의 개수뿐이다.
            </span>
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="arc-takeaway">
          <span class="arc-takeaway-label"><span class="lang-en">Takeaway</span><span class="lang-ko">핵심 한 줄</span></span>
          <span class="lang-en">MHA, GQA and MQA are one dial — how many query heads share
            each cached K/V — and turning it changes only the cache, not the attention
            math.</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">MHA·GQA·MQA는 하나의 다이얼 — cache된 K/V 하나를 몇 개의
            query head가 공유하는가 — 이고, 다이얼을 돌려도 바뀌는 것은 attention 수식이
            아니라 cache뿐이다.</span>
        </div>
        <p class="arc-question">
          <span class="lang-en">A 4× or 32× smaller cache sounds abstract — what does it buy
            in gigabytes on real model configs?</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">cache가 4×, 32× 작아진다는 말은 추상적이다 — 실제 모델
            config에서 몇 GB를 아끼는 걸까?</span>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ §4 · KV-BYTES CALCULATOR ============ -->
    <section class="section-tight" id="arc-s4">
      <div class="container">
        <h2 class="viz-h arc-heading">
          <span class="arc-num">§4</span>
          <span class="lang-en">KV-bytes calculator</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">KV-byte 계산기</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="arc-bridge">
          <span class="lang-en">We have the dial and we have the formula. What is still
            missing is scale: whether sharing heads saves megabytes or tens of gigabytes
            depends on the other factors — layers, context, dtype. This calculator puts
            shipped configs through the formula so you can watch each term move.</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">다이얼도 공식도 손에 있다. 아직 없는 것은 규모 감각이다:
            head 공유가 몇 MB를 아끼는지 수십 GB를 아끼는지는 나머지 인자 — layers,
            context, dtype — 에 달려 있다. 이 계산기는 실제 출시된 config를 공식에 넣어
            각 항이 움직이는 것을 보여준다.</span>
        </p>
        <p class="viz-sub">
          <span class="lang-en">Pick a real model or move the sliders; the bars compare what
            the four variants would cache for the same backbone shape.</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">실제 모델 preset을 고르거나 slider를 움직여 보자. 막대는 같은
            backbone 형상에서 네 방식이 각각 cache하게 될 양을 비교한다.</span>
        </p>

        <div class="viz-frame">
          <div class="pre-row" role="group" aria-label="Model presets">
            <button class="pre-chip" data-pre="0" type="button">Llama-2-7B · MHA</button>
            <button class="pre-chip on" data-pre="1" type="button">Llama-3-8B · GQA</button>
            <button class="pre-chip" data-pre="2" type="button">Mistral-7B · GQA</button>
            <button class="pre-chip" data-pre="3" type="button">DeepSeek-V2 · MLA</button>
