          <p class="cap" id="mlaCap">
            <span class="lang-en">Multi-head Latent Attention in one picture: instead of
              caching per-head K and V, DeepSeek-V2 caches one 512-dim latent c^KV plus one
              64-dim RoPE key per token — everything else is rebuilt, or folded into other
              weight matrices, at compute time. Step through to see how.</span>
            <span class="lang-ko">Multi-head Latent Attention 한눈에 보기: head별 K·V를
              cache하는 대신 DeepSeek-V2는 token마다 512-dim latent c^KV와 64-dim RoPE key
              하나만 cache한다 — 나머지는 계산 시점에 복원되거나 다른 weight matrix에
              흡수된다. Step을 넘기며 확인해 보자.</span>
          </p>

          <noscript>
            <p class="viz-sub">
              <span class="lang-en">With JavaScript the diagram is a 7-step walkthrough;
                without it you see the full dataflow at once.</span>
              <span class="lang-ko">JavaScript가 있으면 7단계 walkthrough로 동작하며, 없으면
                전체 dataflow가 한 번에 표시된다.</span>
            </p>
          </noscript>
        </div>

        <div class="prose">
          <p>
            <span class="lang-en">
              MQA and GQA still cache keys and values — just fewer of them. MLA caches a
              different object: a 512-dim low-rank latent from which per-head K and V are
              linearly reconstructed. Because the reconstruction is linear, W<sup>UK</sup>
              folds into the query path and W<sup>UV</sup> into W<sup>O</sup> offline, so
              per-head K/V never materialize at decode time. The one obstacle is RoPE: a
              position-dependent rotation between W<sup>UK</sup> and the latent would make
              the folded product change every step. DeepSeek's fix is to carry position in a
              separate 64-dim key, shared across heads, and add the two dot products — the
              "decoupled RoPE" that costs 64 extra cached elements and saves the whole trick.
            </span>
            <span class="lang-ko">
              MQA와 GQA는 여전히 key·value를 cache한다 — 개수만 줄일 뿐이다. MLA는 cache하는
              대상 자체가 다르다: head별 K·V를 선형으로 복원할 수 있는 512-dim low-rank
              latent다. 복원이 선형이기 때문에 W<sup>UK</sup>는 query 경로에,
              W<sup>UV</sup>는 W<sup>O</sup>에 offline으로 흡수(absorption)되어 decode
              시점에는 head별 K/V가 아예 실체화되지 않는다. 유일한 걸림돌이 RoPE다:
              position에 의존하는 회전이 W<sup>UK</sup>와 latent 사이에 끼면 흡수된 곱이
              step마다 달라진다. DeepSeek의 해법은 position 정보를 모든 head가 공유하는
              별도의 64-dim key에 실어 두 dot product를 더하는 것 — cache 원소 64개를 더
              내고 트릭 전체를 살리는 "decoupled RoPE"다.
            </span>
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="arc-takeaway">
          <span class="arc-takeaway-label"><span class="lang-en">Takeaway</span><span class="lang-ko">핵심 한 줄</span></span>
          <span class="lang-en">MLA changes <em>what</em> is cached, not how much of it:
            a shared low-rank latent plus a 64-dim position key, made viable by linear
            weight absorption — 576 elements per layer, whatever the head count.</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">MLA는 '얼마나'가 아니라 <em>무엇을</em> cache하는가를
            바꾼다: 공유 low-rank latent와 64-dim position key — 선형 weight absorption이
            이를 가능하게 하고, head 수와 무관하게 layer당 576개 원소면 된다.</span>
        </div>
        <p class="arc-question">
          <span class="lang-en">That is the mechanism. But does all this sharing cost
            quality — what do the papers actually measure?</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">메커니즘은 여기까지다. 그런데 이런 공유가 품질을 깎지는
            않을까 — 논문들은 실제로 무엇을 측정했나?</span>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ §6 · TRADE-OFF PANEL ============ -->
    <section class="section-tight" id="arc-s6">
      <div class="container">
        <h2 class="viz-h arc-heading">
          <span class="arc-num">§6</span>
          <span class="lang-en">What the papers actually claim</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">논문이 실제로 주장하는 것</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="arc-bridge">
          <span class="lang-en">The mechanism is settled; the remaining question is
            evidence. Sharing K/V is only a good trade if quality survives it — here is
            what each paper claims, in its own words, with the arithmetic behind each
            headline number.</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">메커니즘은 정리됐다. 남은 질문은 근거다. K/V 공유는 품질이
            살아남을 때에만 좋은 거래다 — 각 논문이 자기 표현으로 주장하는 내용과, 헤드라인
            수치 뒤의 산수를 모았다.</span>
        </p>
        <p class="viz-sub">
          <span class="lang-en">Published quality-vs-memory evidence only — qualitative where
            numbers aren't independently verified.</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">공개된 quality-vs-memory 근거만 담았다 — 독립 검증되지 않은
            수치는 정성적으로만 서술한다.</span>
        </p>

        <div class="card-grid to-grid">
          <div class="card">
            <h3>MHA <span class="to-year">2017</span></h3>
            <p>
              <span class="lang-en">The reference point. Every head keeps a private K/V pair,
                so cache traffic scales with the full head count: at Llama-2-7B shape that is
                512 KB per token — 4 GB of cache at 8K context before batching.</span>
              <span class="lang-ko">기준점. 모든 head가 전용 K/V pair를 가지므로 cache가
                전체 head 수에 비례한다. Llama-2-7B 형상에서는 token당 512 KB — batching
                이전에 8K context만으로 4 GB다.</span>
            </p>
            <span class="ev-chip">2 · 32 L · 32 kv · 128 · 2 B = 512 KB/token</span>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <h3>MQA <span class="to-year">Shazeer 2019</span></h3>
            <p>
              <span class="lang-en">One K/V head serves every query head. The paper's claim:
                decoding is much faster because the K/V tensors shrink by the head count, with
                “only minor quality degradation” — the aggressive endpoint of the dial.</span>
              <span class="lang-ko">하나의 K/V head가 모든 query head를 담당한다. 논문의
                주장: K/V tensor가 head 수만큼 줄어 decoding이 크게 빨라지고 품질 저하는
                “only minor quality degradation” 수준 — 다이얼의 가장 공격적인 끝점이다.</span>
            </p>
            <span class="ev-chip">arXiv 1911.02150 · 32× smaller cache vs MHA-32</span>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <h3>GQA <span class="to-year">Ainslie et al. 2023</span></h3>
            <p>
              <span class="lang-en">Groups of query heads share K/V heads. Uptraining T5-XXL
                with 8 KV groups for just 5% of pre-training compute gave “quality close to
                multi-head attention with comparable speed to MQA” — the result that made
                8-group GQA the open-model default (Llama-3, Mistral).</span>
              <span class="lang-ko">query head들이 그룹 단위로 K/V head를 공유한다. T5-XXL을
                8개 KV group으로 pre-training compute의 5%만 들여 uptraining하자 “quality
                close to multi-head attention with comparable speed to MQA” — 이 결과가
                8-group GQA를 open 모델의 기본값(Llama-3, Mistral)으로 만들었다.</span>
            </p>
            <span class="ev-chip">arXiv 2305.13245 · GQA-8, α = 0.05 uptraining</span>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <h3>MLA <span class="to-year">DeepSeek-V2 2024</span></h3>
            <p>
              <span class="lang-en">All heads share one low-rank latent. The paper reports a
                93.3% KV-cache reduction versus DeepSeek 67B, a cache “equal to GQA with only
                2.25 groups”, and — in its own ablations — quality above MHA. That last claim
                is paper-reported; treat it as the authors' measurement, not settled fact.</span>
              <span class="lang-ko">모든 head가 하나의 low-rank latent를 공유한다. 논문은
                DeepSeek 67B 대비 93.3%의 KV cache 절감, “GQA 2.25 group과 동일한” cache,
                그리고 자체 ablation에서 MHA보다 높은 품질을 보고한다. 마지막 주장은 저자
                측정치이므로 확정된 사실이 아니라 논문 보고 수치로 받아들이자.</span>
            </p>
            <span class="ev-chip">arXiv 2405.04434 · 576 elts/layer/token</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="arc-takeaway">
          <span class="arc-takeaway-label"><span class="lang-en">Takeaway</span><span class="lang-ko">핵심 한 줄</span></span>
          <span class="lang-en">GQA-8's near-free 4× cut (5% uptraining compute) made it the
            open-model default; MLA's stronger claims — 93.3% smaller cache, quality above
            MHA — are author-reported and worth reading as such.</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">거의 공짜인 GQA-8의 4× 절감(uptraining compute 5%)이 open
            모델의 기본값을 만들었다. MLA의 더 강한 주장 — 93.3% 작은 cache, MHA 이상의
            품질 — 은 저자 보고 수치이므로 그렇게 읽어야 한다.</span>
        </div>
        <p class="arc-question">
          <span class="lang-en">If the head factor is this compressible, what is left — and
            which factor does the field attack next?</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">head 인자가 이렇게까지 압축된다면 남은 것은 무엇이고, 이제
            field는 어느 인자를 공략하고 있을까?</span>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ §7 · WHERE THIS GOES ============ -->
    <section class="section" id="arc-s7">
      <div class="container">
        <h2 class="viz-h arc-heading">
          <span class="arc-num">§7</span>
          <span class="lang-en">Where this goes — the other two levers</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">어디로 가는가 — 남은 두 개의 레버</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="arc-bridge">
          <span class="lang-en">The head factor is one lever of three, and the field's
            frontier is less about pushing any single lever further than about composing
            them — and about porting MLA-style caches beyond the models they were born
            in.</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">head 인자는 세 레버 중 하나일 뿐이고, field의 최전선은 어느
            한 레버를 더 미는 것보다 레버들을 합성하는 쪽 — 그리고 MLA류 cache를 태생 모델
            바깥으로 이식하는 쪽 — 에 있다.</span>
        </p>

        <div class="eff-note band-dark">
          <h3>
            <span class="lang-en">Why the KV cache is the axis that matters</span>
            <span class="lang-ko">왜 KV cache가 핵심 축인가</span>
          </h3>
          <p>
            <span class="lang-en">
              Decoding is memory-bound: each generated token must read the weights plus the
              entire KV cache of every preceding token, and the cache — not compute — is what
              caps batch size on a fixed-memory GPU. Head sharing is one of three orthogonal
              levers on the same bytes: this page's axis shrinks the <em>head</em> factor
              (MHA → MQA/GQA → MLA), quantization shrinks the <em>bytes-per-element</em>
              factor, and hybrid/linear attention attacks the <em>sequence-length</em> factor.
              Because they multiply, they compose: a GQA model with a quantized cache, or an
              MLA model inside a hybrid stack, pays the product of the discounts.
            </span>
            <span class="lang-ko">
              decoding은 memory-bound다: token 하나를 생성할 때마다 weight 전체에 더해 앞선
              모든 token의 KV cache를 읽어야 하고, 고정 메모리 GPU에서 batch 크기를 막는
              것은 연산이 아니라 cache다. head sharing은 같은 byte에 걸린 세 개의 직교
              레버 중 하나다: 이 페이지의 축은 <em>head</em> 인자를 줄이고(MHA → MQA/GQA →
              MLA), quantization은 <em>bytes-per-element</em> 인자를, hybrid/linear
              attention은 <em>sequence length</em> 인자를 공략한다. 곱으로 작용하므로 서로
              합성된다: cache를 quantize한 GQA 모델, hybrid stack 안의 MLA 모델은 할인율의
              곱을 그대로 가져간다.
            </span>
          </p>
          <div class="eff-chips">
            <span class="eff-chip">bytes = 2 · layers · kv_heads · head_dim · b/elt · L</span>
            <span class="eff-chip">heads × bits × length — three multiplying levers</span>
            <span class="eff-chip">MLA: 576 elts/layer, whatever the head count</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="prose">
          <p>
            <span class="lang-en">
              Each lever is an active research front. On the <em>bytes</em> axis, KV-cache
              quantization pushes stored precision down to 4 and even 2 bits — see the
              reviews of <a href="/reviews/kivi/">KIVI</a>,
              <a href="/reviews/kvquant/">KVQuant</a> and
              <a href="/reviews/turboquant/">TurboQuant</a>. On the <em>length</em> axis,
              eviction and hybrid designs keep only the tokens or heads that matter —
              <a href="/reviews/h2o/">H2O</a>,
              <a href="/reviews/duo-attention/">DuoAttention</a>, and hybrid stacks like
              <a href="/reviews/minimax-01/">MiniMax-01</a> or linear-attention lines such as
              <a href="/reviews/gated-deltanet/">Gated DeltaNet</a>. Questions the papers
              themselves leave hanging: how the levers behave when composed — a latent is a
              different object from a key, so per-axis results don't automatically stack —
              and whether pretrained MHA/GQA models can be converted to MLA-style caches
              cheaply instead of training from scratch.
            </span>
            <span class="lang-ko">
              레버 하나하나가 살아 있는 연구 전선이다. <em>bytes</em> 축에서는 KV-cache
              quantization이 저장 정밀도를 4-bit, 심지어 2-bit까지 내린다 —
              <a href="/reviews/kivi/">KIVI</a>, <a href="/reviews/kvquant/">KVQuant</a>,
              <a href="/reviews/turboquant/">TurboQuant</a> 리뷰 참고. <em>length</em>
              축에서는 eviction과 hybrid 설계가 중요한 token·head만 남긴다 —
              <a href="/reviews/h2o/">H2O</a>,
              <a href="/reviews/duo-attention/">DuoAttention</a>, 그리고
              <a href="/reviews/minimax-01/">MiniMax-01</a> 같은 hybrid stack이나
              <a href="/reviews/gated-deltanet/">Gated DeltaNet</a> 같은 linear-attention
              계열. 논문들이 스스로 남겨 둔 질문들: 레버들을 합성하면 어떻게 되는가 —
              latent는 key와 다른 대상이므로 축별 결과가 자동으로 곱해지지 않는다 — 그리고
              pretrained MHA/GQA 모델을 처음부터 다시 학습하지 않고 MLA류 cache로 싸게
              변환할 수 있는가.
            </span>
          </p>

          <h3>
            <span class="lang-en">Going deeper</span>
            <span class="lang-ko">더 깊이 가기</span>
          </h3>
          <ul class="deeper-list">
            <li><a class="arrow-link" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1911.02150" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Fast Transformer Decoding: One Write-Head is All You Need — MQA (Shazeer, 2019)</a></li>
            <li><a class="arrow-link" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.13245" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GQA: Training Generalized Multi-Query Models from Multi-Head Checkpoints (Ainslie et al., 2023)</a></li>
            <li><a class="arrow-link" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.04434" target="_blank" rel="noopener">DeepSeek-V2 — Multi-head Latent Attention (2024)</a></li>
            <li><a class="arrow-link" href="/study/models/hybrid-attention/">Hybrid attention — removing the sequence-length axis</a></li>
            <li><a class="arrow-link" href="/reviews/kivi/">KIVI review — quantization, the orthogonal bytes-per-element axis</a></li>
            <li><a class="arrow-link" href="/study/quantization/kv-quant-dataflow/">KV-cache quantization, byte by byte</a></li>
          </ul>
          <p class="fine-print">
            <span class="lang-en">Configs verified against official sources (July 2026):
              Llama-2-7B (32 layers, 32Q/32KV, hidden 4,096), Llama-3-8B and Mistral-7B-v0.1
              (32 layers, 32Q/8KV), DeepSeek-V2 (60 layers, 128 heads, kv_lora_rank 512,
              qk_rope_head_dim 64), DeepSeek-V3 (61 layers, otherwise same MLA dims). Mistral
              v0.1's sliding-window attention is not modeled by the calculator. Quality
              claims are quoted from the respective papers.</span>
            <span class="lang-ko">config는 공식 소스로 검증했다(2026년 7월): Llama-2-7B
              (32 layers, 32Q/32KV, hidden 4,096), Llama-3-8B·Mistral-7B-v0.1 (32 layers,
              32Q/8KV), DeepSeek-V2 (60 layers, 128 heads, kv_lora_rank 512,
              qk_rope_head_dim 64), DeepSeek-V3 (61 layers, 나머지 MLA 차원 동일). Mistral
              v0.1의 sliding-window attention은 계산기에 반영하지 않았다. 품질 주장은 각
              논문에서 인용했다.</span>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

